  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Potential for patchy frost Saturday night and \nMonday night across the north.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure will be building in this evening from Canada. \nMovement of the high will determine how low temps can drop \nSaturday night into Sunday morning. Confidence in frost \npotential has decreased due to ensemble models pointing to a \nthicker cloud deck much earlier in the evening. Upper air model \nsoundings indicate the weak winds at the surface with lower\nsurface dewpoints. Thus, lower RH values which should keep \nfrost potential low. Due to the uncertainty, kept frost in the \nforecast for consistency.\n\nCold front moves through Monday with high pressure building in\nrapidly behind. This should allow winds over the valleys to\ndecouple under clear skies over the north. Only caveat to frost\nformation will be fairly dry dewpoints expected with Canadian\nhigh.",
